name: Lesson report records preserve acceptance, source limits and explicit format omissions
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py seed @TMP_TARGET @ART
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: lessons
require-live-snap: 25 Labeled accepted lesson | recorded-lessons
expect: Labeled retired lesson
ask: Does the lesson list preserve accepted and retired records as separate historical guidance without changing the finding decision?
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Lessons: exports preserve | report-loading
keys: s
require-live-snap: 25 workspace history | report
expect: workspace history
ask: Does Report describe linked current lesson records and source-revision limits without claiming a fix or complete repository coverage?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 sarif · 1 finding(s) | sarif-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py sarif @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 markdown-bundle · all | bundle-selection
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 markdown-bundle · 1 finding(s) | bundle-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py bundle @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 jsonl · all | jsonl-selection
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 jsonl · 1 finding(s) | jsonl-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py jsonl @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 json · all | json-selection
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 json · 1 finding(s) | json-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py json @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Are the actual export outcomes visible, with exact accepted and retired revisions preserved in the native files and no model work?
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 Lessons: omitted | csv-omissions
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 csv · 1 finding(s) | csv-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py csv @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Is omission visible before CSV export, with alternatives that preserve the lesson records?
resize: 160x48
keys: Home
live-snap: report-160x48
resize: 96x89
keys: Home
live-snap: report-96x89
resize: 80x24
keys: Home
live-snap: report-80x24
resize: 60x20
keys: Home
live-snap: report-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: report-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
require-live-snap: 20 Lessons: omitted | report-lessons-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: report-middle-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: report-middle-later-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: report-controls-40x12
expect: Enter export again
ask: Can operators read the format, destination, lesson omissions and export controls by keyboard across all six viewports?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Lessons: exports preserve | recovered-report-loading
keys: s
require-live-snap: 25 Lessons: exports preserve | recovered-report
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/lesson_report.py restart @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the same lesson and finding decisions while keeping format/source limits visible and making no model request?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
